  "feature_instruction": "The Order Management feature handles the complete lifecycle of customer food orders, from creation and payment processing to status updates and retrieval. It integrates with the `menu-management` feature to fetch `MenuItem` details and with a pre-scaffolded `PaymentService` for payment processing. \n\n**Data Models:**\n*   `Order.java`: Represents a customer's order, containing a unique ID, customer details (user ID, name, address, phone), order date, total amount, current status, and a list of `OrderItem`s. It also includes fields for payment details (transaction ID, payment status).\n*   `OrderItem.java`: Represents a single item within an `Order`, linking to a `MenuItem` (via `menuItemId`), storing the quantity, and the price at the time of order.\n*   `OrderStatus.java`: An enum defining the possible states of an order: `PENDING`, `CONFIRMED`, `OUT_FOR_DELIVERY`, `DELIVERED`, `CANCELLED`.\n\n**Repositories:**\n*   `OrderRepository.java`: Provides standard CRUD operations for `Order` entities and custom queries to find orders by `userId`.\n*   `OrderItemRepository.java`: Provides standard CRUD operations for `OrderItem` entities.\n\n**Services:**\n*   `OrderService.java`: Orchestrates the order creation and management process. \n    1.  `createOrder(CreateOrderRequest request, UUID userId)`: \n        *   Validates the `CreateOrderRequest`. \n        *   Fetches `MenuItem` details for each `OrderItemRequest` from `menu-management`'s `MenuService.getMenuItemById(UUID id)`. If any `MenuItem` is not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException`.\n        *   Calculates the total amount of the order.\n        *   Creates a new `Order` entity with `PENDING` status and saves it using `OrderRepository.save()`.\n        *   Creates `OrderItem` entities for each item in the request and saves them using `OrderItemRepository.saveAll()`.\n        *   Initiates payment by calling `PaymentService.createOrder(new CreatePaymentRequest(amount, \"INR\", \"order_\" + order.getId()))`. \n        *   If payment creation fails, throw `OrderProcessingException`.\n        *   Updates the `Order` with the `paymentTransactionId` and `paymentStatus` from the `PaymentOrderResponse`.\n        *   Returns an `OrderResponse`.\n    2.  `getOrdersByUserId(UUID userId)`: Retrieves all orders for a specific user from `OrderRepository` and maps them to `List<OrderResponse>`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if no orders are found for the user.\n    3.  `getOrderById(UUID orderId)`: Retrieves a single order by its ID from `OrderRepository` and maps it to an `OrderResponse`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the order is not found.\n    4.  `getAllOrders()`: Retrieves all orders from `OrderRepository` (for admin use) and maps them to `List<OrderResponse>`.\n    5.  `updateOrderStatus(UUID orderId, OrderStatus newStatus)`: Updates the status of an order. \n        *   Retrieves the `Order` by `orderId`. Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found.\n        *   Updates the `status` field of the `Order` entity.\n        *   Saves the updated `Order` using `OrderRepository.save()`.\n        *   Returns the updated `OrderResponse`.\n\n**Controllers:**\n*   `OrderController.java`: Provides public API endpoints for authenticated users to create and view their own orders.\n    *   `POST /api/v1/orders`: Creates a new order. Expects `CreateOrderRequest` in the request body. The `userId` is extracted from the authenticated user's context.\n    *   `GET /api/v1/orders`: Retrieves all orders for the authenticated user.\n    *   `GET /api/v1/orders/{orderId}`: Retrieves a specific order by ID for the authenticated user.\n*   `AdminOrderController.java`: Provides admin-only API endpoints for managing all orders.\n    *   `GET /api/v1/admin/orders`: Retrieves all orders in the system.\n    *   `GET /api/v1/admin/orders/{orderId}`: Retrieves a specific order by ID.\n    *   `PUT /api/v1/admin/orders/{orderId}/status`: Updates the status of an order. Expects `UpdateOrderStatusRequest` in the request body.\n\n**DTOs:**\n*   `CreateOrderRequest.java`: Contains `List<OrderItemRequest>` and `deliveryAddress` (String), `customerName` (String), `customerPhone` (String).\n*   `OrderItemRequest.java`: Contains `menuItemId` (UUID) and `quantity` (Integer).\n*   `OrderResponse.java`: Contains `id` (UUID), `userId` (UUID), `customerName` (String), `customerPhone` (String), `deliveryAddress` (String), `orderDate` (LocalDateTime), `totalAmount` (BigDecimal), `status` (OrderStatus), `paymentTransactionId` (String), `paymentStatus` (String), and `List<OrderItemResponse>`.\n*   `OrderItemResponse.java`: Contains `menuItemId` (UUID), `menuItemName` (String), `quantity` (Integer), `unitPrice` (BigDecimal).\n*   `UpdateOrderStatusRequest.java`: Contains `status` (OrderStatus).\n\n**Exceptions:**\n*   `OrderProcessingException.java`: A custom runtime exception thrown when an error occurs during order creation or payment processing, e.g., payment gateway issues or invalid order data.\n\n**Error Handling:**\n*   `ResourceNotFoundException` (from `shared-backend`) will be thrown by `OrderService` if an `Order` or `MenuItem` is not found. Controllers will catch this and return HTTP 404 Not Found.\n*   `OrderProcessingException` will be thrown by `OrderService` for issues during order creation or payment. Controllers will catch this and return HTTP 400 Bad Request.\n\n**Payment Integration:**\n`OrderService` interacts with the pre-scaffolded `PaymentService`. The `PaymentService` is expected to have the following methods:\n*   `createOrder(CreatePaymentRequest request)`: Initiates a payment order with the gateway. `CreatePaymentRequest` contains `amount` (BigDecimal), `currency` (String, always "INR"), `receipt` (String, typically "order_" + orderId).\n*   `PaymentOrderResponse`: Contains `id` (String, payment gateway's order ID), `status` (String), `amount` (BigDecimal), `currency` (String), `receipt` (String), `attempts` (Integer), `notes` (Map<String, String>), `createdAt` (Long).\n\n**Security:**\n*   Customer-facing endpoints (`/api/v1/orders/**`) require authentication.\n*   Admin-facing endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/orders/**`) require admin authentication.",
  "depends_on_features": [
    "menu-management",
    "shared-backend"
  ],
